    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d884">

                <pb facs="0848" n="744" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg744"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/6408.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul at Nuevo
                            Laredo to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Nuevo Laredo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-02-27T17:00:00-06:40">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 27, 1913—5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A peace commission will meet in Nuevo Laredo this evening, composed of the
                    following persons: Lieut. Manuel Carea Aldape, Delio Marcus Canton, Perrajon
                    Lupez, José M. Garza, Ramon and Ricardo Garcia Granados, representing the States
                    of Sonora, Chihuahua, Nuevo Leon, Coahuila, and Tamaulipas. The object of the
                    meeting is to agree on a basis for permanent peace for Mexico.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Garrett</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
